<Project>

  <!-- SP-0093: hold the WPF runtime back from 10.0.11, which breaks MediaElement network audio.

       Symptom: every station fails instantly. MediaElement raises MediaFailed with an
       InvalidOperationException while the server answers 200, so the application opens, loads the
       catalog, and plays nothing at all. Module traces show the broken build stopping after MFPlat and
       never loading mfnetcore.dll, the Media Foundation *network* source; a working build loads the
       whole MFCORE / mfnetcore / mfsrcsnk chain.

       Isolated by swapping only the WindowsDesktop runtime underneath one unchanged published build:
         PresentationCore 10.0.1126.37416  (runtime 10.0.11)  fails
         PresentationCore 10.0.1026.32716  (runtime 10.0.10)  reaches AUDIO LIVE
         PresentationCore 10.0.926.27113   (runtime 10.0.9)   reaches AUDIO LIVE
       The published 26.0820.1828 release carries 10.0.11 and is affected, so this pin is what makes the
       next release playable rather than a precaution.

       Why it lives here and not in the project file. The runtime pack version is carried by
       KnownFrameworkReference items, which the .NET SDK defines in its own targets - imported after
       every line of a project's body. Directory.Build.targets is imported later still, so this is the
       first place the item exists to be updated. Two earlier attempts are recorded so they are not
       retried: the global RuntimeFrameworkVersion property is inherited by Microsoft.Windows.SDK.NET.Ref
       too, whose versions look like 10.0.19041.57, and restore dies with NU1102 hunting a "10.0.10" of
       it; and RuntimeFrameworkVersion metadata on a FrameworkReference item is silently ignored - it
       builds, and ships 10.0.11 anyway.

       Removing the pin: delete this file once a runtime past 10.0.11 is confirmed fixed. Confirm by
       publishing and launching with a live station URL on the command line and watching for AUDIO LIVE,
       never on the strength of a version number. -->

  <!-- Unconditional on purpose: every project here targets net10.0, so there is no other
       KnownFrameworkReference row to protect. Revisit if a second target framework is ever added. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <KnownFrameworkReference Update="Microsoft.WindowsDesktop.App"
                             DefaultRuntimeFrameworkVersion="10.0.10"
                             LatestRuntimeFrameworkVersion="10.0.10" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
